# Corpus unit adaptive-pruning/C04 — gap (unmet mandatory variance CQ, annotator-optional),
# with the derived-arithmetic leg certificate-checked (issue #57)
#
# Source: m0/annotations/adaptive-pruning.yaml C04 (causal, component_ablation; corpus pin
# 62e9b54). Headline: removing the kurtosis (outlier-aware) salience term from APT drops the
# LLaMA2-7B four-task OpenLLM average from 50.0 to 38.1 at 30% sparsity — a 23.8% relative drop
# ((50.0 - 38.1) / 50.0) — so the kurtosis term is critical for large-LM pruning (E03, Table 5).
#
# Lowering notes (conventions: corpus-units/LOWERING.md):
#   * component_ablation family; conclusion contributes(kurtosis_salience, apt_llama2_7b,
#     openllm_avg). single_variable (E03 step 6 omits only the kurtosis term) and protocol_parity
#     (E03 steps 7/8 test at fixed 30% sparsity, E02 fixes the eval harness) are annotated met.
#   * variance_reported is annotated UNMET-GAP: E03 reports single runs (no seeds/repeats). The
#     annotator rated this CQ OPTIONAL, reasoning the 23.8% relative effect makes noise an
#     unlikely full explanation; corpus-v1 makes variance mandatory family-wide (uniform-standard
#     rule, adaptive-pruning/C03), so the policy call wins and the mandatory obligation has no
#     discharging leaf. No complete component_ablation instance is declarable — E2-style gap.
#   * Divergence from test-time-model-adaptation/C04: there variance had NO annotated CQ, so
#     margins licensed a discharge; here the annotator explicitly evaluated variance and rated it
#     unmet, so no honest margins-discharge is available — the claim lands `gap`, not `justified`.
#   * The '23.8% reduction' arithmetic and the 5%-relative falsification threshold ARE now
#     certificate-checked (annotation strict_certifier: domain-checker(rational-arithmetic);
#     issue #57): sub-claim c04a carries the derived identity rel_drop_ge(50, 38.1, 0.238, 0.05)
#     supported by the strict Family-10 rule under an ra@1 certificate — the two score cells
#     enter as premise leaves (e4/e5), the certificate names those slots and carries the drop as
#     the exact fraction 119/500, and the backend recomputes (50 - 38.1) / 50 = 119/500 = 0.238
#     >= 0.05 in exact rational arithmetic. Numerals use CANONICAL spellings (`50`, not `50.0`)
#     per the Family-10 exception to the constants-only rule (canon = id caveat).
#   * c04a is intentionally NOT statused: the unit's queried claim stays the headline c04 (one
#     claim-support instance per unit, m0/sample.tsv grain). The strict step is measured through
#     the compiled AF (a1 in) and the #56 aggregator's load-bearing scan, not through a second
#     status row. The certificate discharges ONLY the arithmetic identity relative to the cited
#     cells — the truth of the cells stays with the defeasible observed leaves (factivity
#     firewall), and the headline ablation claim itself remains gap exactly as before.
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact adaptive-pruning at sha256:de3685165a53
policy corpus-v1
use backends [nd@1, ra@1]

# --- The headline claim, stated but not assemblable at corpus-v1's evidential bar --------------

claim c04
  nl      = "Removing the kurtosis (outlier-aware) salience term from APT drops the LLaMA2-7B four-task OpenLLM average from 50.0 to 38.1 at 30% sparsity, a 23.8% relative drop, so the kurtosis term is critical for large-LM pruning"
  formal  = contributes(kurtosis_salience, apt_llama2_7b, openllm_avg)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = reviewed }

# --- The certificate-checked derived-arithmetic sub-claim (issue #57) ---------------------------

claim c04a
  nl      = "The kurtosis ablation's OpenLLM-average drop from 50.0 to 38.1 is a 23.8% relative drop, exceeding the 5% falsification threshold"
  formal  = rel_drop_ge(50, 38.1, 0.238, 0.05)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = reviewed }

# --- Evidence leaves are present ... ------------------------------------------------------------

# Principal premise: E03's kurtosis ablation cells (full 50.0 vs ablated 38.1), per result cell.
leaf e1 : reports(e03, ablation_effect(kurtosis_salience, apt_llama2_7b, openllm_avg, positive))
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E03, Table-5, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N09-N10]

leaf e2 : isolated(kurtosis_salience, e03)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E03-step-6, logic/experiments.md#E03-Setup]

leaf e3 : matched_protocol(e03)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E03-step-7, logic/experiments.md#E02-step-5]

# The two score cells the certificate consults, one leaf per Table-5 cell (per-result-cell
# grain). These carry the raw numbers; their truth is observed evidence, not certified content.
leaf e4 : reports(e03, score_cell(full_config(kurtosis_salience, apt_llama2_7b), openllm_avg, 50))
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E03, Table-5]

leaf e5 : reports(e03, score_cell(ablated_config(kurtosis_salience, apt_llama2_7b), openllm_avg, 38.1))
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E03, Table-5]

# --- ... the derived arithmetic is certificate-checked ... --------------------------------------

# The ra@1 certificate: consults premise slots 0 (full cell) and 1 (ablated cell) and carries
# the claimed drop as the exact lowest-terms fraction 119/500 = 0.238. Replay recomputes
# (50 - 38.1) / 50 exactly and checks 0.238 >= 0.05.
arg a1 : supports(c04a) by rational_drop_recheck(kurtosis_salience, apt_llama2_7b, openllm_avg, e03, 50, 38.1, 0.238, 0.05)
  assurance = cert(ra@1, sha256:corpus-v1-ra-theory-0, (radrop (prem 0) (prem 1) (frac 119 500)))

# --- ... but no complete argument for the headline claim is declarable --------------------------

# (Intentionally no `arg` for c04: variance_reported(e03) has no honest leaf — E03 reports
# single runs — and corpus-v1 makes that obligation mandatory. The headline claim's
# complete-support set is empty.)

status c04

# ==============================================================================================
# EXPECTED VERDICT (golden oracle)
# ==============================================================================================
# Compiled AF: a1 alone (the strict certificate step), unattacked -> in (grounded).
# Claim status:
#   c04 -> gap (empty complete support; statusC = Gap iff null claimSupport, spec §8 — the
#               strict sub-claim's arg supports c04a, not c04)
